>> B2: Describe how file descriptors are associated with open files.
>> Are file descriptors unique within the entire OS or just within a
>> single process?

File descriptors are managed per-process via `struct f_desc`, which pairs an integer
`fd` with a `struct file *`. Each thread holds an independent `fds` list.

File descriptors are unique only within a single process. Each process allocates
descriptors from its own `cur_fd` counter (starting at 2). Two different processes
can have the same descriptor number referring to completely different files.

